53","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/9/#testresult/c50a5427f0db6553","status":"failed","statusDetails":"Failed to setup devices [edge-dev]: rpc error: code = Unknown desc = failed to reconfigure disks for device \"edge-dev\" after installation: failed to detach disk virtio0 from device \"eve-c2c4fcd9-edge-dev\": bad request: 400 Parameter verification failed. - {\"virtio0\":\"unable to apply pending change virtio0 : lvremove 'pve/vm-105-disk-1' error:   Logical volume pve/vm-105-disk-1 in use.\\n\"}\n\nClaude's conclusion:\n### Root cause\n\nThis failure is entirely broker/Proxmox-side, not an EVE/pillar bug — no EVE device ever came up to inspect (`evetest status` shows \"No EVE devices found\", `evetest sdn status` reports the SDN client was never initialized at the point of failure). The timeline from `gotest.json`/broker logs: the installer completed successfully at 22:28:30, Proxmox VM 105 was removed at 22:28:58, and just 5 seconds later (22:29:03) the broker tried to reconfigure the device's disks (detach `virtio0`) as the next step, but Proxmox rejected it with `lvremove 'pve/vm-105-disk-1' ... Logical volume pve/vm-105-disk-1 in use` — i.e., the LVM logical volume backing the just-removed VM's disk hadn't yet been released (device-mapper node still held open) when the very next Proxmox API call tried to act on it. This is a timing race on the shared Proxmox host between VM teardown and the subsequent disk-reconfigure call, exactly the class of broker-side flakiness already called out in this same night's ledger entry for `TestThreeNodesUpgrade` (run #8), which hit different Proxmox symptoms (`unexpected end of JSON input`, `no worker upid`) from host overload during concurrent VM lifecycle operations — not the identical error signature, but the same underlying mechanism (Proxmox host races/overload under rapid VM create/remove/reconfigure cycles). I found no prior occurrence of this specific `lvremove`/\"Logical volume in use\" signature anywhere in `live-ledger.md`, so this particular manifestation is new tonight, though it fits the broader recurring Proxmox-infra-flake pattern documented since at least 2026-11-01.","time":{"start":1793916868000,"stop":1793917865250,"duration":997250}},{"uid":"7cbe28926e8f8913","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/8/#testresult/7cbe28926e8f8913","status":"passed","time":{"start":1793837915000,"stop":1793838796480,"duration":881480}},{"uid":"ed3d2962226b06d1","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/7/#testresult/ed3d2962226b06d1","status":"passed","time":{"start":1793743961000,"stop":1793746120710,"duration":2159710}},{"uid":"6ef27e1fa5150ae2","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/6/#testresult/6ef27e1fa5150ae2","status":"passed","time":{"start":1793658138000,"stop":1793658708200,"duration":570200}},{"uid":"bf04993d1ca98bac","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/5/#testresult/bf04993d1ca98bac","status":"passed","time":{"start":1793579997000,"stop":1793580554610,"duration":557610}},{"uid":"42711b06d11eb082","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/4/#testresult/42711b06d11eb082","status":"passed","time":{"start":1793491294000,"stop":1793491845780,"duration":551780}}]},"tags":[]},"source":"e20a50dc5fed478.json","parameterValues":[]}